<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal plan sees jobless under six pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal plan sees jobless under six pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government expects the country's unemployment rate to fall below six percent by 2000 from just over seven percent at present, a senior finance ministry official said.</p>
<p>Budget secretary Manuela Arcanjo told a news conference that this was one of the aims of the government's 1998-2000 economic plan which was presented on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;(This plan) permits a reduction in the rate of unemployment which it is hoped will be below six percent in 2000,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
